       wwaaddddwwssttrr writes the characters of the (wide-null-terminated) wide-char‐
       acter string _w_s_t_r to the window _w_i_n.  Its process is  similar  to  con‐
       structing a _c_c_h_a_r___t for each _w_c_h_a_r___t in _w_s_t_r, then calling wwaadddd__wwcchh(3X)
       with the resulting _c_c_h_a_r___t.

       •   Spacing and non-spacing characters in the string are processed  one
           at a time, and

       •   control characters are processed as in wwaadddd__wwcchh(3X).

       wwaaddddnnwwssttrr writes at most _n wide characters, or until a terminating wide
       null character occurs in _w_s_t_r.  If _n is -1, wwaaddddnnwwssttrr writes the entire
       wide string.

       nnccuurrsseess(3X) describes the variants of these functions.

