       These functions return OOKK on success and EERRRR on failure.

       X/Open  Curses  does not specify any error conditions.  _n_c_u_r_s_e_s returns
       an error

       •   if the window pointer is NNUULLLL,

       •   if the string pointer is NNUULLLL, or

       •   if an internal wwaadddd__wwcchh(3X) call returns an error.

       Functions prefixed with “mv” first perform cursor movement and fail  if
       the position (_y, _x) is outside the window boundaries.

